* Waveforms of device models, against ngspice's transient (tests/models.mjs, part 1).
* Each bench's pin "in" is driven by the test (a square or a sine); the others are compared.
* A diode's stored charge (TT): reverse recovery, driven ±5 V at 10 kHz through 1 k
.model DRR D(IS=1e-14 N=1 RS=0.5 TT=5u CJO=20p VJ=0.7 M=0.5)
.subckt recovery in k
D1 in k DRR
R1 k 0 1k
.ends
* A saturating transistor switch without transit time: 0 to 5 V at 10 kHz into 4.7 k
.model QSW NPN(IS=1e-14 BF=100 BR=2 CJE=10p CJC=5p RB=20 VAF=100)
.subckt switch in c
Vcc vcc 0 5
Rb in b 4.7k
Q1 c b 0 QSW
Rc vcc c 1k
Cl c 0 20p
.ends
* The same switch whose transistor has a transit time (TF): stored charge delays its turn-off
.model QTF NPN(IS=1e-14 BF=100 BR=2 CJE=10p CJC=5p RB=20 VAF=100 TF=200n TR=2u)
.subckt switchtf in c
Vcc vcc 0 5
Rb in b 4.7k
Q1 c b 0 QTF
Rc vcc c 1k
Cl c 0 20p
.ends
* A CMOS inverter into 1 nF, 0 to 10 V at 10 kHz through 1 k
.model NSW NMOS(LEVEL=1 VTO=1.5 KP=20m LAMBDA=0.01)
.model PSW PMOS(LEVEL=1 VTO=-1.5 KP=10m LAMBDA=0.01)
.subckt cmos in o
Vdd vdd 0 10
Rg in g 1k
Cg g 0 100p
M1 o g 0 0 NSW
M2 o g vdd vdd PSW
Cl o 0 1n
.ends
* A class-B follower clipping into 8 ohm: 1 kHz, 20 V peak through 100 ohm, ±15 V rails
.model QBN NPN(IS=1e-13 BF=80 VAF=100 IKF=3 CJE=200p CJC=100p RB=2 RE=0.05)
.model QBP PNP(IS=1e-13 BF=60 VAF=80 IKF=3 CJE=250p CJC=150p RB=2 RE=0.05)
.subckt classb in b o
Vp vp 0 15
Vn vn 0 -15
Rs in b 100
Q1 vp b o QBN
Q2 vn b o QBP
Rl o 0 8
.ends
* A varactor's charge: a reverse-biased junction (CJO 1 nF) swung hard by a 10 kHz sine through 10 k
.model DVC D(IS=1e-14 CJO=1n VJ=0.7 M=0.5 FC=0.5)
.subckt varactor in k
Vb b 0 12
R1 in k 10k
D1 k b DVC
R2 k 0 100k
.ends
* A power MOSFET switch (VDMOS): 0 to 10 V at 10 kHz through 470 ohm into the gate, 24 V through 47 ohm;
* its gate-drain capacitance grows from CGDMIN to CGDMAX as the drain falls (the Miller plateau)
.model MPW VDMOS(VTO=3.5 KP=5 RD=20m RS=10m CGS=800p CGDMAX=1.5n CGDMIN=40p A=0.5 CJO=500p IS=1e-12)
.subckt vdmos in g d
Vdd vdd 0 24
Rg in g 470
M1 d g 0 MPW
Rd vdd d 47
.ends
* A level 3 power MOSFET switch: 0 to 10 V at 10 kHz through 470 ohm into the gate, 24 V through 47 ohm;
* the gate charge is Meyer's (TOX) plus the overlaps, the drain-bulk junction's capacitance CBD
.model MN3W NMOS(LEVEL=3 VTO=3.2 KP=20.5u THETA=0.05 VMAX=3e5 ETA=0.001 KAPPA=0.4 TOX=100n NFS=6.6e11 PHI=0.6 RS=20m RD=50m CGSO=1.2n CGDO=0.2n CBD=600p PB=0.8 MJ=0.5 IS=1e-12)
.subckt mos3sw in g d
Vdd vdd 0 24
Rg in g 470
M1 d g 0 0 MN3W W=0.3 L=2u
Rd vdd d 47
.ends
* A level 2 CMOS inverter into 20 pF: 0 to 5 V at 100 kHz through 10 k, Meyer gate capacitances
.model MN2W NMOS(LEVEL=2 VTO=0.8 UO=550 TOX=40n NSUB=3e15 UCRIT=5e4 UEXP=0.15 XJ=0.5u LD=0.2u LAMBDA=0.02 CGSO=0.3n CGDO=0.3n CJ=2e-4)
.model MP2W PMOS(LEVEL=2 VTO=-0.8 UO=220 TOX=40n NSUB=5e15 UCRIT=5e4 UEXP=0.15 XJ=0.5u LD=0.2u LAMBDA=0.03 CGSO=0.3n CGDO=0.3n CJ=3e-4)
.subckt cmos2 in g o
Vdd vdd 0 5
Rg in g 10k
M1 o g 0 0 MN2W W=200u L=2u AD=1n AS=1n
M2 o g vdd vdd MP2W W=500u L=2u AD=2.5n AS=2.5n
Cl o 0 20p
.ends
